    "description": "As the CMS, I need to write assignments against a stable key I own and have Salesforce resolve the rep, so sync is idempotent and every Salesforce record traces back to its CMS record.\n\n* Deal_Rep_Assignment\\__c.DRA_External_Id_\\_c — Text(255), External Id, Unique, NOT required (migrated records will not have one)\n\n* Upsert on that key creates or updates correctly; replaying an identical call is a no-op beyond field updates\n\n* Rep resolution follows external Id -> slug -> email, first match wins, and relates the user to the assignment\n\n* Zero or multiple matches set Assignment_Status__c = Review Required with a note recording what was attempted\n\n* The integration user's permission set covers the new field\n\nEffort: 3-5h. Assumes the rep identifier fields on the User record are in place from the sign-up logging build.\n\nSource: CMS Integration Design v1, §5.1 + Appendix A.\n\nNOTE: Appendix A lists this as blocked by D9, but §1.2 commits Jumpr to building it in parallel ahead of Direction 1 so the CMS team has a working sandbox endpoint. Treating as Up Next — D9 only governs the fallback identity approach, not the field itself.",
